package mapdemo

// A map whose VALUE is an ENUM-KEYED ARRAY (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.4, §2.8):
// "A VALUE is anything a table field can hold ... `[E]T`". The value is an
// ordinary field of the generated entry, so its storage is that field's own
// row, `TableKeyed<T, E>` (§4.2), one slot per named variant and no count. That
// is ONE member, so the handle is the slot itself and the keyed array's own
// surface reaches the variants.

table Slots
{
    seats map[int32][Slot]int32 // [E]T: one slot per named variant, under a signed key
    after int32
}
